casebook held-demo v1
source "quorum fixture: time in rules" dated 2026-10-09 by "quorum project"
note "A bearing that runs hot for a moment after a load change is normal; one that STAYS hot is not. The"
note "temperature threshold therefore asserts only after holding for 5 s. Vibration has no hold: a spike above"
note "the extreme limit is itself the emergency. The rulebook is still checked over every state, because time"
note "decides only when a reading becomes true, never what a true reading means."

observe bearing_hot      "bearing temperature high, sustained"
observe vib_extreme      "vibration above the extreme limit"
observe greasing         "lubrication cycle in progress"

channel bearing_temp "bearing temperature" unit degC
  range -20 200
  stale_after 10s
  asserts bearing_hot above 90.0 release 85.0 for 5s

channel vibration "bearing housing vibration" unit mm/s
  range 0 50
  stale_after 5s
  asserts vib_extreme above 11.0 release 10.5

claim overheating "bearing overheating" severity 7 needs bearing_hot
claim seizing     "bearing seizing"     severity 9 needs bearing_hot vib_extreme
excuse grease_heat "grease churning warms the bearing briefly" needs greasing
grease_heat undercuts overheating
vib_extreme rebuts grease_heat

claim blind "a bearing sensor cannot be believed" when any bearing_temp_unavailable vibration_unavailable

action carry_on idle
action inspect when any overheating blind
action trip safe when seizing
prefer trip over inspect over carry_on
